{"author":{"id":"2de4467f26c42fb223f4d3ddd5611e7c0513d3daae4c1dc315de039036bc997d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778954652,"nonce":"LL3JubezyoLkqvrh0gHvtpUCmSk=","title":"Vendor Google fonts to make builds network-independent","message":"The production build currently depends on live Google Fonts fetches through next/font/google in lib/fonts.ts. During verification in a feature worktree, npm run build reached next build and then failed because fonts.googleapis.com could not resolve:\\n\\n- lib/fonts.ts: Failed to fetch Fira Sans from Google Fonts\\n- lib/fonts.ts: Failed to fetch Inter from Google Fonts\\n- lib/fonts.ts: Failed to fetch Roboto from Google Fonts\\n- lib/fonts.ts: Failed to fetch Roboto Mono from Google Fonts\\n- lib/fonts.ts: Failed to fetch Source Serif 4 from Google Fonts\\n\\nBest fix: vendor the required font files or add font packages and switch lib/fonts.ts to next/font/local, preserving the existing CSS variables (--font-inter, --font-roboto, --font-roboto-mono, --font-source-serif, --font-fira-sans). This should be handled separately because it is user-visible typography work and should include a visual comparison after the font files are chosen.","files":null}]}